{"quotes":[{"segments":["So I decided years ago that I wanted to react to “CSS is hard” by getting better at CSS and taking it seriously as a technology, instead of devaluing it. Doing that changed everything for me: I learned that so many of my frustrations (“centering is impossible”) had been addressed in CSS a long time ago, and that also what “centering” means is not always straightforward and it makes sense that there are many ways to do it. CSS is hard because it’s solving a hard problem!"]},{"segments":["The idea here is to organize CSS by “components”, in a way that’s spiritually related to Vue or React components. (though there might not actually be any Javascript at all in the site)

